<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">All Blacks</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1884">1884</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as New Zealand national rugby union team</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The All Blacks are <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a>'s national rugby union team, named for their black kit and known for performing the haka before matches. Since their first international tour in 1884 they have become one of the most successful teams in any sport, winning the Rugby <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fifa-world-cup">World Cup</a> in 1987, 2011 and 2015. Rugby and the team occupy a central place in New Zealand's national identity.</p></div>
